{"The `blacklistedGuestEmails` array is lowercased but the `guest` email being checked is not lowercased before comparison, allowing users to bypass the email blacklist by using different casing": 0.9814898371696472, "The `isTeamAdminOrOwner` variable uses `&&` (AND) but the name and intent indicate `||` (OR). The `isTeamAdmin` function already returns truthy for both ADMIN and OWNER roles, so using `&&` with `isTeamOwner` means team admins who aren't owners are incorrectly denied permission to add guests": 0.9423245191574097, "The `sendAddGuestsEmails` function receives `guests` (the original input) instead of `uniqueGuests` (the filtered list of actually added guests), causing existing attendees to receive `AttendeeScheduledEmail` instead of `AttendeeAddGuestsEmail` when a user tries to add an already-existing attendee's email": 0.9556421637535095, "The `AddGuestsDialog` component passes `setIsOpenDialog` directly to `onOpenChange`, so internal state (`multiEmailValue` and `isInvalidEmail`) is not reset when dialog is closed via X button or clicking outside, showing stale data when reopened": 0.9606780409812927, "The new `MultiEmail` component in `packages/ui/form/MultiEmail.tsx` duplicates existing functionality from `packages/features/form-builder/Components.tsx` instead of extracting the existing one, creating maintenance burden": 0.2279541790485382, "The `ZAddGuestsInputSchema` is defined inside the component function body, causing it to be recreated on every render instead of being defined outside the component or in a shared location": 0.44151943922042847}